  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Demo spine",
      "items": [
        "The workflow begins and ends in the GitHub issue maintainers already use.",
        "Read-only triage proposes a narrow contract before remediation is authorized.",
        "The approved path produces one reviewable pull request rather than merging code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust controls",
      "items": [
        "The controller validates actor permission, issue contract, allowed paths, and an immutable target SHA.",
        "Devin sessions receive no secrets; GitHub and Devin credentials stay with the controller.",
        "Structured output is treated as a proposal and cross-checked against observed pull-request facts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Deterministic proof",
      "items": [
        "Success requires issue linkage, an unchanged base SHA, policy-compliant changed files, and the named CI check.",
        "SQLite records idempotent runs and append-only transitions for restart-safe reconciliation.",
        "The issue comment and report expose session, pull request, CI, elapsed time, ACUs, and terminal outcome."
      ]
    }
